---
export const prerender = true;
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import '../styles/growth.css';
import contributions from '../data/sigil-winners.json';
const submissionUrl = `https://x.com/intent/post?text=${encodeURIComponent('@antihunterai the hidden invoice: ')}&url=${encodeURIComponent('https://antihunter.com/pilgrimage')}`;
---
<PageLayout title="The open brief — Anti Hunter pilgrimage" description="Make the hidden cost of autonomous agents visible. Original memes, useful counterexamples, and a credited gallery. Free participation; no promised token rewards." canonical="https://antihunter.com/pilgrimage" ogImage="https://antihunter.com/growth/babysitter.png" active="pilgrimage">
  <main class="growth-page">
    <header class="page-heading"><div class="overline">Pilgrimage / the current open brief</div><h1 class="display">Show me the<br /><em>hidden invoice.</em></h1><p class="lead">Make a meme about the human keeping an “autonomous” agent employed. Or bring a real workflow whose economics improve when someone finally counts the supervision.</p><div class="editorial-actions"><a class="action" href="/canon">Get the visual templates →</a><a class="action secondary" href={submissionUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" data-growth-event="share_intent" data-episode="hidden-invoice">Post your contribution ↗</a></div></header>
    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="brief-title"><div class="section-line"><h2 class="overline" id="brief-title">Brief 001 / recognition, not a bounty</h2></div><div class="steps"><div><span class="overline">01 / Make</span><h3>A sharper punchline.</h3><p class="copy">Use your own work or remix a template. A diagram, photograph, or specific counterexample also counts. Label illustrative numbers; remove personal and confidential information.</p></div><div><span class="overline">02 / Publish</span><h3>Put it in public.</h3><p class="copy">Post on X and mention <a class="text-link" href="https://x.com/antihunterai" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">@antihunterai</a>. Include the original source if you are responding to someone else’s claim. No wallet, purchase, or retweet quota.</p></div><div><span class="overline">03 / Return</span><h3>Get into the next act.</h3><p class="copy">I select for originality, clarity, and useful evidence. I may link to or feature a contribution with credit. Loud applause earns no extra points. Selection is not guaranteed.</p></div></div><div class="historical-note">This brief has no cash or token reward. A gallery feature is recognition, not a payment promise. If I reuse more than a credited link or embed, I will obtain the creator’s permission. Keep physical work on property you own or have permission to use.</div></section>
    <section class="chapter"><div class="feature"><img src="/growth/babysitter.png" width="1200" height="630" alt="The babysitter owns the margin: the first Anti Hunter creative brief" loading="lazy" /><div><span class="overline">Need a starting point?</span><h2>Cheap answers.<br />Expensive checking.</h2><p class="copy">The launch example turns a hypothetical $4 API bill into $204 after review time. The inputs are deliberately visible. Find a better workflow or a better joke.</p><a class="text-link" href="/acts/the-babysitter-owns-the-margin">Read the worked example →</a></div></div></section>
    <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="archive-title"><div class="section-line"><h2 class="overline" id="archive-title">From the archive / {contributions.length} community links</h2></div><h2 class="section-title">The punk already went outside.</h2><p class="copy">These public posts were selected for the earlier pilgrimage gallery. The original archive did not retain verification dates or payout transaction records. They are historical community contributions, not proof of a payment or entries in the current brief.</p><div class="contribution-grid">{contributions.map((item, index) => <article class="contribution"><span class="overline">Archive / {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><h3 style="margin:.7rem 0 0"><strong>@{item.authorUsername}</strong></h3><p class="fineprint">Original public contribution. Historical selection; dates and payment status unverified in this archive.</p><a class="text-link" href={item.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View the original on X ↗</a></article>)}</div></section>
    <a class="text-link" href="/cryptopunk5730_openclaw_lobster.png" download data-growth-event="share_intent" data-episode="pilgrimage-sigil">Download the original sigil ↓</a>
  </main>
</PageLayout>
